{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188213-tf-v-and-their-theme","id":188213,"title":"TF:V and their theme..","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-04T13:48:48-07:00","id":188213,"title":"TF:V and their theme..","content":"some thought I thought about while re-watching Captain America (don't know if someone already mentioned it)..<br /> <br /> TF:V's turning point was during the WWII, right? When they met the &quot;ENEs&quot; which supported the Nazis. Norse/ German mythology has fascinated those Nazis which were interested in occult. Task Force VALKYRIE use a Norse theme for their weapons and tech. Doesn't anyone finds it a little.. weird? Like, too much of a coincidence?<br /> <br /> Is there a chance something like HYDRA from the Marvel movies is hiding inside TF:V? Or maybe there is something even weirder in the organization? Some dirty secret in the roots if TF:V which the organization is truly ashamed of, even more than its patronizing vampires? Heck, considering that vampires live a very long time, maybe the vampires which now fund VALKYRIE are the same which fund the &quot;nazi occult division&quot; in WoD?<br /> <br /> thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T14:14:11-07:00","id":188230,"title":"","content":"One word: Paperclip. Specifically, Operation Paperclip, the post-war effort to round up German scientists and engineers and bring them to the West under new names. My dad liked to joke that the USA beat the Soviets to the moon because &quot;we had better Nazis,&quot; and it's not far off the mark. <br /> <br /> In the real world, the Thule Society was a bunch of mortal occultists who backed the early Nazi party; they were disavowed once the party took power and quickly faded from relevance. In the World of Darkness, the Thule fellas are already the origin of the Loyalists of Thule, who are ruled by the guilt of what their ancestors did by helping Hitler and his buddies out; wouldn't it make sense for those occultists to have actually had some success? There's no reason to believe that a bunch of interested sorts would turn to the occult as a weapon if they actually had it at their disposal.<br /> <br /> So we have Thule sorcerers and those with a grasp of occult physics/fringe science working under the German war effort, giving the eventual Loyalists something to eventually be <i>really</i> guilty about; it stands to reason that VALKYRIE would be able to pick these men out from the general number of those grabbed by Paperclip and press them into service. Hell, you could even build an entire chronicle around Loyalists lashing out at VALKYRIE for being a &quot;Nazi-fueled government conspiracy&quot; and make a grand time of it.<br /> <br /> (Delta Green had the Thule dealing with some real magic mojo, going on to be a wartime German division of the Ahnenerbe known as the Karotechia. Delta Green came into its own by combating the Karotechia well into the 1950s. Considering that DG and VALKYRIE occupy identical niches as &quot;government anti-supernatural task forces,&quot; I consistently end up thinking that the Karotechia is a part of WoD canon and use them as part of my Loyalists backstory.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}